(a) whether 5G laboratories have been established in academic institutions and if so, the institutions selected;
(b) whether these laboratories are being used to develop applications in agriculture, healthcare, education and smart manufacturing;
(c) whether a roadmap has been formulated to promote indigenous research, innovation, start-ups and 6G technologies;
(d) the financial assistance provided and mechanism for monitoring outcomes; and
(e) whether additional laboratories or centres of excellence are proposed for future communication technologies and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any targeted measures to enhance the participation of tribal women in Van Dhan Vikas Kendras (VDVKs) and allied livelihood activities;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the number of tribal women beneficiaries associated with VDVKs and SHGs supported under the scheme;
(c) whether any initiatives have been undertaken to facilitate skill development, value addition, branding, access to credit and market linkages for tribal women; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen sustainable livelihood opportunities and entrepreneurial capacities of tribal women through the Van Dhan ecosystem?

(a) the major initiatives under White Revolution 2.0 to strengthen dairy cooperatives, enhance milk procurement and promote value addition;
(b) whether priority areas have been identified for expanding dairy cooperative activities, particularly in Maharashtra and Bihar, and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the measures proposed to strengthen dairy infrastructure, promote participation of women and small dairy farmers, and integrate cooperative institutions; and
(d) the expected outcomes in terms of higher farmers' incomes, employment generation and cooperation-led rural development?

(a) whether Government has launched the Strategy for Artificial Intelligence in Healthcare for India (SAHI) and the Benchmarking Open Data Platform for Health AI (BODH) and if so, the features thereof;
(b) the institutional mechanisms under SAHI to ensure ethical, transparent, secure and interoperable use of AI in healthcare;
(c) the manner in which BODH facilitates evaluation and validation of AI models using anonymised real-world datasets; and
(d) whether Government has prepared a roadmap for wider adoption of AI-enabled healthcare solutions, including capacity building, patient data privacy and algorithmic accountability?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the likely impact of recent geopolitical developments in West Asia on MSMEs and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the measures taken to strengthen MSME resilience against supply chain disruptions, raw material price volatility, transportation and logistics challenges and working capital constraints;
(c) whether any framework/mechanism exists for continuous monitoring and timely policy intervention to protect MSMEs from external economic shocks and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to enhance the competitiveness and adaptability of MSMEs amid evolving global uncertainties?

(a) the manner in which the initiatives and commitments under the Indore Declaration will benefit Indian farmers, particularly small and marginal farmers;
(b) whether areas have been identified for gains from BRICS cooperation in digital agriculture, regenerative farming, seed systems and agricultural trade;
(c) whether an action plan has been prepared to facilitate transfer of technologies, best practices and innovations to farmers; and
(d) whether these initiatives are expected to improve farm incomes, reduce input costs and strengthen climate resilience in Indian agriculture?

(a) whether Government has assessed recent overseas evacuation operations, including Operation Ganga, Operation Kaveri and Operation Ajay, to institutionalise a Standard Operating Procedure for future evacuations;
(b) the measures taken to strengthen preparedness for such evacuations, including risk assessment, contingency planning, inter-agency coordination, transport logistics, communication and post-evacuation assistance;
(c) whether systems are proposed for real-time registration and tracking of Indian nationals in vulnerable countries; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen coordination among the Ministry, Indian Missions and other stakeholders for timely evacuation during emergencies?

(a) the current status of the ASMITA League programme, including sports disciplines covered, leagues conducted, women athletes enrolled and its geographical outreach;
(b) whether the programme has been integrated with Khelo India for talent identification and athlete development;
(c) the measures taken to enhance participation of girls and women from rural, tribal, aspirational districts and other underserved regions in Maharashtra and Bihar; and
(d) whether Government proposes to expand the programme through additional sports disciplines, institutional partnerships and competitive opportunities for women athletes?

(a) the additional features introduced under Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) 4.0 as compared to the earlier versions of the scheme and the manner in which these are expected to improve skilling, employment and industry linkage opportunities for the youth;
(b) whether PMKVY 4.0 envisages skilling in emerging technologies such as Artificial Intelligence, drones, robotics, green energy and semiconductor manufacturing; and
(c) whether any assessment has been undertaken to align courses o?ered under PMKVY 4.0 with industry demand and to strengthen placement, apprenticeship and post-training tracking mechanisms and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has evolved any framework for integrating storage facilities created under the World's Largest Grain Storage Plan (WLGSP) with procurement operations, primary processing activities and agricultural marketing networks;
(b) whether digital inventory management, warehouse receipt systems and logistics solutions are proposed to be incorporated in such facilities;
(c) whether any institutional arrangements have been made to enable Primary Agricultural Credit Society (PACS) to generate sustainable revenue streams from the operation of such infrastructure; and
(d) whether any mechanism has been developed for monitoring utilisation levels and assessing the economic viability of these facilities?

(a) whether, with the implementation of Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) in West Bengal, all States and UTs are now covered under the Scheme and whether Government has assessed its implications for achieving Universal Health Coverage;
(b) the details of inter-State portability availed under AB-PMJAY since inception, particularly by migrant workers and their families, including beneficiaries from Maharashtra and Bihar;
(c) whether Government proposes to strengthen portability and digital integration under the scheme; and
(d) the awareness measures undertaken to inform eligible beneficiaries, migrant workers, about portability provisions?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the growing popularity of online Yoga instruction and digital Yoga coaching platforms;
(b) whether any study has been undertaken to assess the potential of such digital platforms in promoting Yoga as a tool for preventive healthcare, public wellness and global outreach;
(c) whether Government proposes to develop a framework for collaborating with certified Yoga institutions, practitioners and digital platforms to promote authentic and quality-assured Yoga instruction through online modes; and
(d) the details of the initiatives taken or proposed in this regard?

(a) the policy framework regulating Government intervention in domestic airfares during exceptional circumstances;
(b) the criteria, parameters and institutional mechanism adopted for identifying situations warranting such intervention;
(c) the instances during the last three years where Government intervened in domestic airfares, including the reasons for intervention, routes or sectors covered, duration and nature of measures taken; and
(d) the procedure for determining, implementing, monitoring and reviewing such interventions, including the role of Government and the Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA)?

(a) the steps taken to promote startups in fuel-tech, manufacturing and other emerging technology sectors;
(b) whether Government has established partnerships with industry, research institutions, public sector undertakings and private entities to achieve these objectives, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the support proposed under such collaborations, including mentorship, innovation challenges, investor connect, pilot opportunities and market access; and
(d) the number of startups expected to get benefit and the mechanism to assess outcomes?

(a) whether Government has assessed the rise in first-time passport applicants from Tier-2 and Tier-3 cities for education, employment, business and travel abroad;
(b) the measures taken to improve passport and consular services through expansion of PSKs, POPSKs, e-passports and faster passport issuance and police verification;
(c) whether additional facilitation, awareness, digital handholding and simplified compliance measures are proposed; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen grievance redressal through MADAD, CPGRAMS and citizen outreach for students, migrant workers and overseas travelers?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the progress of construction of National High-Speed Corridors and Greenfield Expressways during 2026 and if so, the details thereof;
(b) State-wise status of ongoing and completed National High-Speed Corridor and Expressway projects, including the length awarded, under construction and completed so far;
(c) whether any measures have been taken to expedite completion of delayed highway and expressway projects through revised implementation mechanisms or contractual reforms; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has prepared a roadmap under the National Vision for Cold Water Fisheries 2030 for augmenting production, value addition and marketing of cold-water fish species;
(b) whether any model framework has been evolved for supporting States in developing cold-water fisheries infrastructure;
(c) whether Government proposes to encourage adoption of emerging technologies for strengthening supply chains and improving market access for fish farmers in remote and mountainous regions; and
(d) whether any assessment has been undertaken regarding the potential of cold-water fisheries in reducing imports of fish varieties?

(a) the year-wise budgetary allocation, expenditure and progress made under the Sagarmala Programme since 2022-23, including port modernisation, new port development and coastal infrastructure projects, with State-wise details including Goa;
(b) the increase in port capacity and efficiency & reduction in vessel turnaround time and logistics costs achieved at major and non-major ports;
(c) the status of road, rail and inland waterway connectivity projects undertaken to strengthen last-mile evacuation and seamless multimodal logistics; and
(d) whether Government proposes a unified digital Port Community System with AI-based cargo planning and green port standards to further enhance efficiency, sustainability and global competitiveness?

(a) the details regarding the progress made under the Universal Immunisation Programme and recent initiatives to introduce new vaccines;
(b) the key lessons learned from COVID-19 management and the steps taken to strengthen pandemic preparedness and monitoring/surveillance systems;
(c) the steps taken to strengthen the capacity building of healthcare workers, oxygen infrastructure and critical care facilities; and
(d) the role played by digital tools and data analytics in improving disease monitoring/surveillance and health emergency response systems?

(a) the objective and framework of the Special Assistance to States for Capital Investment (SASCI) Scheme;
(b) the total funds released to the States under the scheme since its inception;
(c) whether this scheme includes any component linked to reforms; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the manner in which Government proposes to strengthen quality assurance and regulatory compliance in AYUSH products being made available through digital commerce platforms;
(b) the role envisaged for the Ayush Export Promotion Council in identifying manufacturers and ensuring adherence to prescribed standards, including the AYUSH Quality Mark framework; 
(c) whether any mechanism exists to support AYUSH MSMEs in accessing digital marketplaces while ensuring compliance with safety, authenticity and labelling norms; and
(d) the steps taken to promote responsible dissemination of verified information on AYUSH products and systems through public-private collaborations with digital platforms?

(a) progress made in implementation of First Mile Connectivity (FMC) projects, including number of projects commissioned, under implementation and proposed as on date;
(b) whether targets under the Coal Logistics Plan and Policy, 2030 have been achieved, particularly with regard to rail connectivity, mechanised coal handling and conveyor-based transportation;
(c) the bottlenecks identified in evacuation of coal from pitheads to end-use destinations, if so, the details thereof;
(d) measures taken to reduce coal logistics costs and improve evacuation efficiency through multimodal transport and dedicated rail infrastructure; and
(e) impact of these initiatives on coal dispatch and timely supply to the power plants and other consuming sectors?

(a) whether Government has introduced the Easy Connect initiative, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the airports identified under the initiative and the timelines envisaged for expansion to major airports;
(c) the details of measures proposed under the initiative, including single-point immigration, airside baggage transfers, dedicated transfer corridors and other facilitation measures to provide seamless transit experience to passengers; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to encourage Indian airports and airlines to emerge as preferred transit points for international passengers and enhance India's position as a global aviation hub?
